@page "/components/ai/conversationlist"
@inherits AppComponentBase

<PageOutlet Url="components/ai/conversationlist"
            Title="AiConversationList"
            Description="BitAiConversationList is the sidebar of AI chat threads, grouped by recency - today, yesterday, the previous seven and thirty days, then by month - with new, switch and delete." />

<DemoPage Name="AiConversationList"
          SecondaryNames="@(["ThreadList"])"
          Description="BitAiConversationList is the sidebar list of conversations, grouped by recency the way people think about them: today, yesterday, the previous seven days, the previous thirty days, then by month. It lists the BitAiConversationSummary records it is given, marks the open one, and raises OnSelect, OnNew and OnDelete - where the conversations are kept, and what switching does, is the app's."
          Parameters="componentParameters"
          SubClasses="componentSubClasses"
          CssVariables="componentCssVariables"
          GitHubAIUrl="ConversationList/BitAiConversationList.razor"
          GitHubDemoUrl="AI/ConversationList/BitAiConversationListDemo.razor">
    <NotesTemplate>
        <BitText>
            To use this component, you need to install the
            <BitLink Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Bit.BlazorUI.AI" Target="_blank">
                <BitTag Reversed
                        Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI"
                        Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground"
                        IconName="@BitIconName.NavigateExternalInline" />
            </BitLink>
            nuget package, as described in the Optional steps of the
            <BitLink Href="/getting-started">Getting started</BitLink> page.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            The list needs no session: hand it summaries - <b>BitAiConversation.ToSummary()</b>, or the
            <b>ListAsync</b> of an <b>IBitAiConversationStore</b> (<b>ai.UseConversationStore&lt;T&gt;()</b>, an in-memory one
            ships with the package) - and switch the chat yourself on <b>OnSelect</b>. The
            <BitLink Href="/ai/scenarios/conversations">conversations</BitLink> scenario puts it over a store, with replies that
            keep streaming in a thread you switched away from.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            The list is a <b>nav</b> named by its <b>AriaLabel</b> or the Conversations string, each group is a list named by its
            heading, the open conversation is marked with <b>aria-current</b> (and set apart by more than its color), and each
            delete button is named after its conversation. A conversation's preview is its tooltip. The words - the new button,
            the group headings, "Untitled" - come from the string table of the
            <BitLink Href="/components/ai/optionsprovider">BitAiUiOptions</BitLink> in force.
        </BitText>
    </NotesTemplate>
    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example1CsharpCode" Id="example1">
            <div>
                <b>Conversations</b> are grouped by how recently they changed, newest first; <b>SelectedId</b> marks the open
                one and <b>OnSelect</b> reports a choice. <b>ShowNewButton</b> takes the new-conversation button away.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div style="max-width:18rem">
                <BitAiConversationList Conversations="summaries"
                                       SelectedId="@selectedId"
                                       OnSelect="HandleSelect"
                                       ShowNewButton="false" />
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>Open: <b>@selectedId</b></div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="New & delete" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example2CsharpCode" Id="example2">
            <div>
                The new-conversation button raises <b>OnNew</b>, and a delete button beside every conversation - shown only
                while <b>OnDelete</b> is set - raises it with the conversation. Both leave the list to the app, which hands it
                the new set of summaries.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div style="max-width:18rem">
                <BitAiConversationList Conversations="editableSummaries"
                                       SelectedId="@editableSelectedId"
                                       OnSelect="HandleEditableSelect"
                                       OnNew="HandleNew"
                                       OnDelete="HandleDelete" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="With a chat" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3">
            <div>
                What it is for: a sidebar beside a <BitLink Href="/components/ai/chat">BitAiChat</BitLink>. Each thread keeps a
                session of its own, so switching is pointing the chat at another session; a thread joins the list once its first
                message arrives, titled after it. Send something, press New, and switch between them.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(9rem, 14rem) minmax(0, 1fr);gap:1rem;height:440px">
                <BitAiConversationList Conversations="chatSummaries"
                                       SelectedId="@chatSession?.Conversation.ConversationId"
                                       OnSelect="SelectChat"
                                       OnNew="NewChat"
                                       OnDelete="DeleteChat" />
                @if (chatSession is not null)
                {
                    <BitAiChat @key="chatSession.Conversation.ConversationId"
                               Session="chatSession"
                               EmptyTitle="New conversation"
                               EmptyBody="Send a message and this thread joins the list." />
                }
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example4CsharpCode" Id="example4">
            <div>
                A disabled list stays readable, with the open conversation marked, and takes no choice, new or delete.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div style="max-width:18rem">
                <BitAiConversationList Disabled
                                       Conversations="summaries"
                                       SelectedId="@selectedId"
                                       OnSelect="HandleSelect"
                                       OnNew="HandleNew"
                                       OnDelete="HandleDelete" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
            <div>
                <b>Style</b> / <b>Class</b> reach the root, <b>Styles</b> / <b>Classes</b> each part (the new button with the
                class-styles of BitActionButton, the group headings, the lists, the items, the item buttons and the selected
                one, the titles and the delete buttons with the class-styles of BitButton). The public
                <b>--bit-AiConversationList-*</b> variables (see the CSS variables table) re-skin it from <b>:root</b>, an
                ancestor or <b>Style</b>.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div style="display:grid;gap:1rem;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr))">
                <BitAiConversationList Conversations="summaries"
                                       SelectedId="@selectedId"
                                       OnSelect="HandleSelect"
                                       ShowNewButton="false"
                                       Style="border-radius:1rem;background:var(--bit-clr-bg-sec)"
                                       Styles="@(new() { GroupHeader = "color:var(--bit-clr-pri)", SelectedItemButton = "font-weight:bold" })" />
                <BitAiConversationList Conversations="summaries"
                                       SelectedId="@selectedId"
                                       OnSelect="HandleSelect"
                                       ShowNewButton="false"
                                       Class="custom-threads"
                                       Classes="@(new() { ItemButton = "custom-threads-item", SelectedItemButton = "custom-threads-selected" })" />
                <BitAiConversationList Conversations="summaries"
                                       SelectedId="@selectedId"
                                       OnSelect="HandleSelect"
                                       ShowNewButton="false"
                                       Style="--bit-AiConversationList-gap:0.25rem;--bit-AiConversationList-padding:0.5rem;--bit-AiConversationList-group-color:var(--bit-clr-pri);--bit-AiConversationList-item-radius:1rem;--bit-AiConversationList-item-color:var(--bit-clr-fg-sec);--bit-AiConversationList-item-background:var(--bit-clr-bg-sec);--bit-AiConversationList-item-hover-background:var(--bit-clr-bg-ter);--bit-AiConversationList-selected-color:var(--bit-clr-pri-text);--bit-AiConversationList-selected-background:var(--bit-clr-pri);--bit-AiConversationList-selected-hover-background:var(--bit-clr-pri-hover)" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6">
            <div>Use BitAiConversationList in right-to-left (RTL).</div>
            <br />
            <div dir="rtl" style="max-width:18rem">
                <BitAiConversationList Dir="BitDir.Rtl"
                                       Conversations="rtlSummaries"
                                       SelectedId="@rtlSelectedId"
                                       OnSelect="HandleRtlSelect"
                                       ShowNewButton="false" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>
</DemoPage>
